      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I understand it, this symbol is not allowed. I sincerely apologize for not noticing it earlier. However, I have a question: would it be possible to add all disallowed symbols to build/kernel/abi/symbols.deny, similar to kernel_write, filp_open, etc.? This way, when I run tools/bazel run //common:kernel_aarch64_abi_update, it would trigger a build error, which could also help make your review process easier.",
      "parentUuid": "575ff5a2_5c8365f7",
      "revId": "36df373103056b703b8346d3ae70841874d6c403",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
